    {
      "id": 227855,
      "name": "starkenburg_alexander",
      "username": "starkenburg_alexander",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/starkenburg_alexander/{size}/1857_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-06-25T19:24:37.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Fine after two rough games.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Focusing down the gladiators seem to be the way to go for me. Lifeline getting the Seeker first turn helps with that, and it slows down the favor gain for each that you drop. I used Comodora to damage boost Fanatic and discard the one gladiator that redirects damage, which helped. Side effect from that is Fixed Point will then save your ongoings and equipment. Another fixed point is you can use concealed assailant without destroying the cloak and without discarding for comodora.&nbsp;Ignore the Pangolin, as he gets chaos lord and will play cards.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>If you can survive to round 3, you get a Fickle Fans, which brought it from 19-5 to 14-10 for me. If you can keep surviving to round 4, you get another Fickle Fans, which brought it back to 12-15 I think. From there, I flipped Kaargra and wailed on gladiators enough for 5 more points and won, with very low hp all around.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>~Komori</p>",
